course: dictionary
lesson: 3493
title: Faraway or far away?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Faraway means a long distance away. «Sound spreads out in every direction and gets weaker with distance, so a faraway shout is faint.» The word tells you the shout comes from a long way off, which is why it sounds quiet.
explain: Check where the word sits. Before a noun, write it as one word: a faraway shout, a faraway land. After a verb, write it as two words: the ship sailed far away. Ask yourself: is it describing something (one word), or telling where something went (two words)?
explain: Faraway can also describe a look. A faraway look means someone is dreaming and not paying attention. Context helps here: a child staring out of the window and not hearing her name has a faraway look, even though she has not gone anywhere.
fact: Faraway means a long distance away.
fact: Before a noun, write «faraway» as one word, as in «a faraway shout».
fact: After a verb, write «far away» as two words.
fact: A faraway look means someone is dreaming and not paying attention.
fact: The Mountains of the Moon is an old name for faraway mountains at the edge of the known world.
exercise: «Sound spreads out in every direction and gets weaker with distance, so a faraway shout is faint.» What does faraway mean here? | Very close and loud | Happy and smiling | Brightly coloured | *A long distance away
exercise: The ship sailed ___ over the sea. Which spelling is right? | farway | faraway | *far away | faraaway
exercise: Mia stares out of the window and does not hear her name. Her teacher says she has a ___ look. Which word fits? | Tidy | Loud | Hungry | *faraway
test: «A blurry or faraway photo is not real proof.» What does faraway mean here? | *A long distance away | Hidden in a box | Brand new | Very bright
test: We walked ___ from home before the rain started. Which spelling is right? | *far away | faraaway | farway | faraway
exam: The news shows the worst things from all over the world, which can make ___ danger feel close. Which word fits best? | hidden | *faraway | far away | close
